    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for python-pypdf",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for python-pypdf fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in python-pypdf:\n\n- CVE-2026-119209: negative /Index values and multiplied xref\n  streams can lead to clamp bypass and server memory exhaustion\n  (bsc#1288950)\n- CVE-2026-119208: trusting forged /Count values in encrypted PDF\n  page trees can lead to excessive resource consumption and denial\n  of service (bsc#1288951)\n- CVE-2026-119207: nested exception text accumulation in strict\n  mode parsing can lead to memory amplification and application\n  denial of service (bsc#1288952)\n- CVE-2026-119206: repeated sequential /Nums scanning in\n  page_labels resolution can lead to algorithmic complexity attacks\n  and denial of service (bsc#1288944)\n- CVE-2026-119205: misdirected reference tracking during dictionary\n  cloning can lead to cycle-detection bypass and thread-hanging\n  infinite loops (bsc#1288943)\n- CVE-2026-119204: unbounded resource entry copying during\n  page-tree flattening can lead to excessive memory allocation and\n  denial of service (bsc#1288942)\n- CVE-2026-119203: unterminated trailer search in incomplete\n  cross-reference tables can lead to an infinite loop and\n  thread-blocking denial of service (bsc#1288941)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
